WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.630
- My wife and I are big
"American Idol" fans.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.880
We go way back, so I'm really feeling

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.871
a little star struck
and insecure right now.

00:00:06.871 --> 00:00:07.704
- The Kelly squared.

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:09.058
The Kelly squared happening right now.

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:09.891
- The Kelly squared, yes.

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:12.150
- There's a lot of
personality sitting here.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.320
- We are both actually
very similar I think.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.150
- We are, well Texas and Carolina.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.110
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes, and bubbly yeah.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.453
We're Southern, we're good girls.

00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:21.490
We both started on "Idol."

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.323
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:22.323 --> 00:00:24.410
- And I had no idea until
literally last night,

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.847
that one of your audition songs was

00:00:25.847 --> 00:00:26.740
"Since You've Been Gone."

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.021
- [Kelly] Yes, oh my gosh!

00:00:28.021 --> 00:00:29.130
- I love that, I didn't know that!

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.640
- Yes, well big fan.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.960
- Oh well, thank you.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.520
- But no, I remember auditioning,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.190
you know there's so
many different rounds--

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.500
- Before you even get to the--

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.130
- Before you even get to
Paula, Randy and Simon,

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.025
which we had the original three.

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:42.740
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh my gosh!

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:43.573
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:00:43.573 --> 00:00:45.487
Time doesn't slow down for nobody does it?

00:00:45.487 --> 00:00:46.320
(Kelly Clarkson laughs)

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.110
You go in, do um,

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.247
I actually auditioned with

00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:51.020
"The Sweetest Thing" by Juice Newton.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.870
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.690
- [Kelly] Went through to the next round,

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.070
and then sang that one
again and I thought,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.324
maybe this will be good,
keep doing this one,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:02.250
and I think it was Paula had asked me

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.960
to sing something, "Could
you sing something pop?"

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.343
And I just started singing your song.

00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:09.260
- That's so funny.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.060
- And I was terrified because--

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.233
- You picked, I mean I
gotta be real with you,

00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:15.794
that would not be my
go-to for an audition.

00:01:15.794 --> 00:01:16.688
(laughs)

00:01:16.688 --> 00:01:18.610
That's a hell of a song!
- I mean, I didn't know,

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.443
and you were the first
person that came to mind.

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:21.750
And then just 20 seconds
of something else,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.650
and so I sang "Broken
Wing" by Martina McBride.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.365
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh
good song, good pick!

00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:26.680
They had me do the same thing.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:27.571
They had all of us do

00:01:27.571 --> 00:01:28.404
- different songs.
- You're like a good luck

00:01:28.404 --> 00:01:29.237
charm for me.

00:01:29.237 --> 00:01:30.070
It got me through to the next round.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.250
- Well, that's awesome.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.610
They had all of us do that though.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.960
Everybody thinks it's like one song.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.126
I had to sing like three different ones

00:01:35.126 --> 00:01:36.220
even to get.
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.550
- I was like, am I still proving

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.070
that I can sing on key here?

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:39.903
What's happening, what?

00:01:39.903 --> 00:01:42.590
- This is amazing backstage dish

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.647
from "American Idol!"

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.770
We are spilling the tea today.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.603
- We are!

00:01:47.603 --> 00:01:48.705
- It's everywhere.

00:01:48.705 --> 00:01:51.130
(Kelly Clarkson laughs)

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.860
- So, I heard we also
have something in common,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:53.860
you eloped right?

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:54.840
- Yes.
- My husband and I eloped.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.673
- That's right.

00:01:55.673 --> 00:01:56.506
- He had a whole plan.

00:01:56.506 --> 00:01:57.730
- Oh my gosh, us too.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.530
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah and then ah, nope.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.470
- We had this whole big wedding planned

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.960
in Nashville and the only thing

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.640
we had failed to do was
send invitations out.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.190
So I'm looking at the guest list--

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.023
- Wait, what?

00:02:11.023 --> 00:02:12.080
So this wasn't on purpose?

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.620
You forgot to invite people?

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.056
- No, I'm getting to
it, so we had this list

00:02:18.056 --> 00:02:21.757
and I'm going, "Hell, I don't even like

00:02:21.757 --> 00:02:22.753
"half of these people

00:02:22.753 --> 00:02:24.740
"and I don't even know the rest."

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.180
You know, because you invite this person

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.190
and that person and then
you gotta, it becomes

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.506
this big ordeal.
- That is exactly why

00:02:30.506 --> 00:02:31.339
I canceled my wedding.

00:02:31.339 --> 00:02:33.640
- And it felt like a CMA
after party, you know?

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.473
- Yes!

00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:35.440
(audience laughs)

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.460
I'm just like, this big production.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.810
- And it's supposed to
be about your moment.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.666
- Yeah, so I said, "Baby,
let's just run away,"

00:02:40.666 --> 00:02:43.050
and he goes, "Whew,
thought you'd never ask."

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.730
So we didn't tell
anybody and just ran off.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.040
- That's so awesome,
he was sweet about it.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:48.873
That's so good.

00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:50.300
- It was so perfect for us.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.440
Everybody has to do what's right for them.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.590
- I will say, you had a very
rare honeymoon location.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:57.563
- We did.

00:02:57.563 --> 00:02:58.640
- You were in Baghdad?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.784
- That's right, well,
that's the place to go now.

00:03:00.784 --> 00:03:02.740
(everyone laughs)

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.890
Great deals on flights.

00:03:04.798 --> 00:03:08.640
(Kelly Clarkson laughs)

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.924
I've been working with
the USO for many years

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:15.700
and I was booked to go
on one early January,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.680
so we said I do and then hopped on a plane

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.050
and flew overseas to Iraq and yeah.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:21.883
- Wow.

00:03:21.883 --> 00:03:22.897
- We spent our honeymoon there.

00:03:22.897 --> 00:03:24.944
- It's amazing.

00:03:24.944 --> 00:03:29.400
- All the soldiers at each
spot that we would stay at,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.410
had a honeymoon suite for us.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.550
It was the funniest thing,
we had a ball though.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:35.420
We wouldn't have changed it.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.800
- Oh my gosh, that's so sweet.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.010
That's cool that you followed through,

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:38.900
it is very important.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.080
They sacrifice a lot for us.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.490
- Say what you mean, mean what you say

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.750
and honor your word.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.340
- Get it South!

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.715
I love it.

00:03:45.715 --> 00:03:47.947
- Well that's when that
sass comes out, I guess.

00:03:47.947 --> 00:03:48.780
(audience applauds)

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.510
But yeah, we've been blessed to be a part

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.861
troop USA tours.

00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:52.694
- What about your wedding?

00:03:52.694 --> 00:03:53.527
Did y'all elope or did
you have a big wedding?

00:03:53.527 --> 00:03:54.980
- We had a secret wedding in our backyard

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.570
with 25 people.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.230
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's amazing.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.851
- Mostly people that
were on your list, so.

00:04:00.851 --> 00:04:03.176
(everyone laughs)

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.009
- I'm sorry.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.510
- There were some country music brass,

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.690
no, we just, we had the same thing

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:09.870
where we just said, you know what?

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.760
Let's not do the big to do.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.390
Let's just keep it very small

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.730
and in fact, it was a surprise wedding.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.590
It was the night before the Emmy's and

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.870
Meghan was nominated, so
we had our families come

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.010
and we just had 'em over

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.647
and we said, "Oh, by the way, if you step

00:04:24.647 --> 00:04:26.697
"into the backyard, this is our wedding."

00:04:27.597 --> 00:04:29.715
- What, that's the coolest thing ever.

00:04:29.715 --> 00:04:32.000
- That's great, yes.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:32.833
- How did y'all meet again?

00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:33.970
How did you and Meghan meet?

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.110
- We met doing a play in Los Angeles.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.440
She was a couple years
into "Will and Grace"

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.110
and I was living in
somebody's basement and--

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.330
- And she was like, "Yes."

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:48.232
- She was like, "Yeah, I'm
sick of classy individuals."

00:04:48.232 --> 00:04:50.403
Let me find a carpenter.

00:04:50.403 --> 00:04:52.790
- (laughs) That's awesome.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.230
- Kelly, tell us about your movie,

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.290
it's "Mistletoe Secret" right, Hallmark?

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.900
- I play a small town
girl from North Carolina,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.590
so it wasn't far of a stretch, you know.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:05.400
And, I'm trying to save my little town

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.320
and bring small businesses,
help them come back to life

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.340
and bring tourists there.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.220
There's a love interest that
comes into play, of course.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.300
- [Kelly Clarkson] Of course,
I'd expect nothing less.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.560
- And so much drama because
it's Hallmark, you know?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.393
- Yeah, I love it.

00:05:18.393 --> 00:05:21.293
- No, it's a sweet little
love story and I get to--

00:05:21.293 --> 00:05:23.900
- That's why I love those
movies, they feel good.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.450
- They're feel good movies, right.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.950
They all have happy endings, so I love it.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.240
- So not like life (laughs)

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.150
- I know right?

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.750
That's why I'm like, oh is this the way

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.230
Christmas is supposed to be?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.094
(laughs)

00:05:35.094 --> 00:05:36.794
- It's very different at my house.

